  "output": "**Result: no release checklist file exists in the workspace.** I searched exhaustively before concluding:\n\n**Searches performed:**\n1. Directory listing of `/home/agent/workspace` (including hidden files): only `.gitignore` and `.kuma/` metadata.\n2. Content search for the term \"checklist\" across all files: **0 matches in 0 files**.\n3. Filename search for any file matching `*check*` or `*release*`: **no results**.\n4. Full recursive file inventory excluding `.kuma/`: just one file, `.gitignore` (9 bytes, containing only `/.kuma/`).\n\n**What I cannot do:** I cannot read or summarize the required items of an existing checklist, because there is no checklist file to read. I will not fabricate one.\n\n**What this finding means:**\n\n- The teammate's report (\"the release checklist cannot be completed because a required file is missing\") is consistent with what I see, but the situation is actually more severe: **the checklist document itself is missing**, in addition to whatever file it references.\n- If the checklist were expected to live in this workspace, it was never added, or it was lost before the workspace was handed over. A `git log` cannot help because there is no git repository here (no `.git` directory).\n\n**Likely candidates for the \"missing required file\"** once the checklist is reconstructed: the workspace has no source code, no `CHANGELOG.md`, no version file, no build artifacts, and no release notes. Any of these could be the blocker.\n\n**Recorded status:**\n- Existing release checklist: **absent**\n- Required items: **unknown/unverifiable** without the original document\n- Candidate missing files: changelog, version manifest, source files, release notes\n\nI can proceed to the next step (identifying the missing file and its impact on the original checklist) based on this inventory, and then propose a revised checklist built strictly from the files that actually exist (currently only `.gitignore`).",
